From fd1885309623220eaa009323334a00b2fe8e5192 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emdee52 <emdee7101@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 14:45:01 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(AS-1): toggle free-Z placement from a plate-column
 button

The free-Z placement key had Preferences as its only UI. Give it a button in
the plate column instead, between the "move plate to the front" up-arrow and
the Snap & Drag magnet, so it sits where the objects it affects are.

  - PartPlate: FREE_Z_HOVER_ID = 10, GRABBER_COUNT 10 -> 11; the icon takes
    the slot the dual-only filament map leaves empty on single-extruder
    printers (slot 6), so the column no longer shows a blank square there.
    Snap & Drag moves to slot 7 / 8 accordingly, and the circular-bed
    centering count follows.
  - Plater: the click toggles orca_ext_free_z (app key + OrcaExt::set_free_z)
    and repaints, which also un-dims the Snap & Drag panel.
  - Icons: plate_freez* (off: part + gravity arrow) and plate_freez_on*
    (on: part floating above the bed), following the plate_locked tile
    convention for idle/hover/active.
  - Preferences: the AS-1 checkbox is removed; the key is unchanged, so an
    existing value still applies.

[ORCAPORT:AS-1]
